WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.225
Lesson 1.4.

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:04.735
Tokens, approvals & allowances.

00:00:04.735 --> 00:00:06.420
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.204
be able to read an approval request

00:00:08.204 --> 00:00:09.690
and know what you're allowing.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.280
Here's the plan.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.965
First, the key ideas.

00:00:13.965 --> 00:00:16.680
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.205
Then, your checklist.

00:00:18.205 --> 00:00:20.367
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.698
can also represent positions (e.g.

00:00:23.698 --> 00:00:26.377
concentrated LP). allowance. The protocol

00:00:26.377 --> 00:00:27.442
then pulls

00:00:27.442 --> 00:00:30.417
tokens when you act. of that

00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:32.862
token, now and in future.

00:00:32.862 --> 00:00:34.703
If the contract (or the

00:00:34.703 --> 00:00:37.612
approval) is exploited, the tokens

00:00:37.612 --> 00:00:40.277
can be taken. off-chain signature,

00:00:40.277 --> 00:00:43.757
not a transaction. There's no gas, so

00:00:43.757 --> 00:00:45.887
they're easy to sign

00:00:45.887 --> 00:00:48.919
without noticing. Drainers abuse exactly this.

00:00:48.919 --> 00:00:50.832
First, most tokens on EVM

00:00:50.832 --> 00:00:54.123
chains are ERC-20 (fungible). NFTs (ERC-721/1155).

00:00:54.123 --> 00:00:55.907
Next, to let a protocol

00:00:55.907 --> 00:01:00.072
move your tokens you approve a spender for an.

00:01:00.072 --> 00:01:02.817
Then, Unlimited approvals are convenient

00:01:02.817 --> 00:01:04.857
but let that contract move

00:01:04.857 --> 00:01:07.558
all. Also, Signature approvals (Permit /

00:01:07.558 --> 00:01:10.097
Permit2) grant allowances with an.

00:01:10.097 --> 00:01:12.477
On top of that, Wrapped / receipt

00:01:12.477 --> 00:01:15.626
tokens: WETH, LP tokens and lending receipts

00:01:15.626 --> 00:01:18.146
represent a claim on something else.

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:22.263
And finally, Fake tokens: anyone can

00:01:22.263 --> 00:01:24.771
create a token called "USDC".

00:01:24.771 --> 00:01:26.971
Only the contract address identifies it.

00:01:28.271 --> 00:01:30.786
Let's work an example, step

00:01:30.786 --> 00:01:33.771
by step. Wallet shows: "Allow 0x3fC9…a1B2

00:01:34.471 --> 00:01:37.519
to spend your U.S.D.C. Amount: Unlimited." Is

00:01:37.519 --> 00:01:41.031
0x3fC9…a1B2 the protocol's official router? Check the

00:01:41.731 --> 00:01:44.956
docs or explorer. Do I need

00:01:44.956 --> 00:01:46.881
unlimited? Edit it to

00:01:46.881 --> 00:01:48.556
the amount of

00:01:48.556 --> 00:01:51.126
this deposit. Is this U.S.D.C.

00:01:51.126 --> 00:01:54.286
the real contract?. After finishing, revoke

00:01:54.286 --> 00:01:57.079
with a revoke tool (for example

00:01:57.079 --> 00:01:59.871
revoke.cash) if I won't be back.

00:02:01.171 --> 00:02:02.631
Here's your checklist.

00:02:02.631 --> 00:02:04.166
Do it now, for real.

00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:07.181
First, Spender verified against official docs.

00:02:07.181 --> 00:02:09.796
Next, Allowance limited to what's needed.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:13.601
Then, Signature requests read as carefully as transactions.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:16.771
And finally, Approvals reviewed and revoked monthly.

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.281
Question 1.

00:02:19.281 --> 00:02:22.116
Why is a gasless "Permit" signature dangerous?

00:02:26.536 --> 00:02:29.596
The answer: It can grant a token allowance without

00:02:29.596 --> 00:02:33.076
a transaction, so it's easy to sign without noticing.

00:02:33.076 --> 00:02:34.936
Drainers use it to take tokens.

00:02:36.236 --> 00:02:37.481
Question 2.

00:02:37.481 --> 00:02:38.424
How do you know a

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.576
token is the real one?

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:46.646
The answer: By its contract address from an

00:02:46.646 --> 00:02:49.416
authoritative source, never by name or ticker.

00:02:50.716 --> 00:02:51.986
Question 3.

00:02:51.986 --> 00:02:53.631
When should you revoke an approval?

00:02:58.051 --> 00:03:00.172
The answer: When you no longer use

00:03:00.172 --> 00:03:02.596
that protocol, or on a regular schedule.

00:03:03.896 --> 00:03:05.141
Let's recap.

00:03:05.141 --> 00:03:09.591
Most tokens on EVM chains are ERC-20 (fungible).

00:03:09.591 --> 00:03:11.554
To let a protocol move your tokens

00:03:11.554 --> 00:03:13.481
you approve a spender for an.

00:03:13.481 --> 00:03:15.827
Unlimited approvals are convenient but

00:03:15.827 --> 00:03:17.751
let that contract move all.

00:03:17.751 --> 00:03:22.196
Signature approvals (Permit / Permit2) grant allowances with an.

00:03:23.496 --> 00:03:26.011
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:26.011 --> 00:03:30.036
